---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Field from '../components/Field.astro';

---
<Base title="Community" description="Where Hale is built and how to take part.">
  <Field />
  <section class="wrap page">
    <div class="page-head">
      <h1>Where Hale is built</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        In the open, on GitHub. The language is early enough that what you
        report still changes it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <ul class="facts">
        <li><b>GitHub</b><p>The compiler, the specification and the pond libraries live under <a href="https://github.com/hale-lang">github.com/hale-lang</a>. Issues and discussions are the channel today. The most useful report is a small, reproducible example of something that fought you.</p></li>
        <li><b>What helps most</b><p>Real programs. Write something in Hale and file an issue where the language or the docs got in your way. The pattern catalog and the standard library grow from concrete use.</p></li>
        <li><b>Before you start</b><p>Read the <a href="/docs">guide</a> and the <a href="/docs/spec/styleguide">style guide</a>, and browse <a href="/packages">pond</a> for the library shapes to mirror.</p></li>
        <li><b>Not yet</b><p>A chat space and a formal contribution guide. Open an issue meanwhile. Early questions are welcome.</p></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
